WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.788
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:16.058 --> 00:19.311
[theme music playing]

3
00:26.527 --> 00:28.320
[liquid bubbling]

4
00:32.658 --> 00:35.327
[clinking, rattling]

5
00:35.453 --> 00:36.579
[cat meows]

6
00:37.496 --> 00:39.623
[hoofbeats]

7
00:41.250 --> 00:42.168
[water splashes]

8
00:49.049 --> 00:51.051
[handcuffs rattling, click]

9
00:55.681 --> 00:56.515
[thumps]

10
00:56.599 --> 00:58.476
[breathing heavily]

11
00:59.059 --> 01:01.187
I haven't confirmed that you've quit yet.

12
01:01.562 --> 01:03.189
You're not going anywhere, okay?

13
01:04.482 --> 01:07.485
No. I won't let you quit.

14
01:08.110 --> 01:10.654
[quirky music playing]

15
01:14.909 --> 01:15.910
[inhales]

16
01:15.993 --> 01:18.871
Do you really think… you'll have a better time working with her?

17
01:18.954 --> 01:19.830
Do you think so?

18
01:20.873 --> 01:22.166
Do you think so?

19
01:22.249 --> 01:23.876
Is that what you think? [sniffs]

20
01:23.959 --> 01:25.252
[executive 1] Um, sir?

21
01:25.336 --> 01:26.295
[executive 2] Sir?

22
01:27.630 --> 01:28.798
Uh…

23
01:31.884 --> 01:33.385
How long have you all been here?

24
01:33.469 --> 01:35.888
Would you like to tell us why you've decided to drop by?

25
01:40.810 --> 01:41.894
Find this person.

26
01:43.187 --> 01:45.397
[executives groaning]

27
01:46.106 --> 01:47.733
You have five minutes. Go now.

28
01:47.817 --> 01:49.068
-Five minutes. Hurry! -[indistinct clamoring]

29
01:49.151 --> 01:51.153
[executive 1] Find him! Find him! What are you standing around for?

30
01:51.237 --> 01:53.030
[man] It's her first time to a theme park.

31
01:53.113 --> 01:54.281
[executive 2] We can find him. Let's go.

32
01:54.365 --> 01:56.700
[man] I never got to bring her to a place like this.

33
01:57.576 --> 01:59.787
Uh, it's her birthday today,

34
01:59.870 --> 02:01.247
and she was hoping to try one of the rides.

35
02:01.330 --> 02:02.498
[staff] I'm really sorry, sir.

36
02:02.581 --> 02:03.791
I wish I could help,

37
02:03.874 --> 02:06.877
but I'm afraid we don't allow entries 30 minutes before closing.

38
02:07.837 --> 02:09.004
Right, I understand.

39
02:14.009 --> 02:15.261
[Jin-hyung] My balloon!

40
02:15.678 --> 02:18.889
-[crowd cheering] -[fireworks exploding, crackling]

41
02:21.100 --> 02:22.184
[Yi-jun] Here you go.

42
02:22.893 --> 02:24.687
-[Jae-hee] Son! -[Jin-hyung] Thank you, sir.

43
02:24.770 --> 02:25.688
Papa!

44
02:26.313 --> 02:27.147
[relieved sigh]

45
02:27.231 --> 02:30.192
I told you you shouldn't run around in a big crowd, son.

46
02:30.276 --> 02:31.694
Son?

47
02:31.777 --> 02:34.446
[dramatic comical music playing]

48
02:34.530 --> 02:35.406
[Jae-hee gasps]

49
02:37.992 --> 02:38.909
Huh?

50
02:40.286 --> 02:41.370
"Papa"?

51
02:41.954 --> 02:45.457
[fireworks crackling]

52
02:46.375 --> 02:48.043
[Jin-hyung] Who are you, mister?

53
02:50.170 --> 02:52.548
Tell me first. Who are you, kid?

54
02:52.631 --> 02:54.008
Do you know my papa?

55
02:54.091 --> 02:56.260
You first. Are you Kang Jae-hee's son?

56
02:56.343 --> 02:57.928
I asked you first, mister.

57
02:58.012 --> 02:59.388
Well, I'm more curious than you.

58
03:01.056 --> 03:03.809
Papa, this man's acting strange.

59
03:03.893 --> 03:05.060
Is he a weirdo?

60
03:05.144 --> 03:08.439
Well, honey, when you run into someone strange,

61
03:08.939 --> 03:10.441
what did I say you should do?

62
03:10.524 --> 03:12.443
You said I shouldn't go with them.

63
03:13.444 --> 03:15.905
But this strange man seems to know you.

64
03:15.988 --> 03:17.156
Is he like you, a poli--

65
03:17.239 --> 03:18.407
Your mom must be waiting, right?

66
03:19.283 --> 03:20.618
-[Jin-hyung] Huh? -Let's go find her.

67
03:20.701 --> 03:22.077
-[Jin-hyung] Uh-huh. -[Jae-hee] Let's go!

68
03:23.078 --> 03:24.496
[Jae-hee shouts] Mama!

69
03:25.122 --> 03:26.081
"Mama"?

70
03:27.082 --> 03:29.251
Kang Jae-hee, you were married?

71
03:29.335 --> 03:31.462
[breathing heavily] Sheesh.

72
03:34.673 --> 03:37.051
Sorry to trouble you, but thanks a lot.

73
03:37.885 --> 03:39.094
You know, Jin-hyung,

74
03:39.637 --> 03:41.764
you look more and more like Sergeant Go.

75
03:43.641 --> 03:44.808
[chuckles softly]

76
03:44.892 --> 03:45.935
Son,

77
03:46.977 --> 03:49.396
next time we meet, I want you two centimeters taller.

78
03:49.480 --> 03:51.273
Okay. Promise.

79
03:51.357 --> 03:53.692
Promise? There. [chuckles softly]

80
03:54.902 --> 03:56.570
[gasps] What's this?

81
03:56.654 --> 03:58.238
[chuckles softly] Thank you.

82
03:58.322 --> 03:59.865
-Bye, Papa. -Bye.

83
03:59.949 --> 04:01.241
Coming at you fast!

84
04:01.325 --> 04:03.118
-[both] Yeah! -[chuckles]

85
04:03.577 --> 04:05.162
-[Jae-hee] Take care. -Okay.

86
04:06.622 --> 04:07.957
[Jae-hee chuckles softly]

87
04:13.420 --> 04:15.589
[Jin-hyung] Thanks for playing with me, Papa.

88
04:16.048 --> 04:17.800
Let's play again.

89
04:17.883 --> 04:21.053
That strange man doesn't seem like a bad person.

90
04:29.103 --> 04:30.187
[sighs]

91
04:30.270 --> 04:32.481
Want me to start, or do you want to explain yourself first?

92
04:32.564 --> 04:34.066
-[executive 1] Sir, we found him! -[executive 2] Sir!

93
04:34.149 --> 04:35.109
[executives] Sir!

94
04:35.192 --> 04:36.318
-We found… -[executives panting]

95
04:36.402 --> 04:37.236
He's here?

96
04:38.028 --> 04:39.029
[executive 2] Um…

97
04:39.113 --> 04:41.407
-What? -[executives exclaiming]

98
04:41.490 --> 04:42.908
-[executive 1] Sir! -[executive 2] Mr. Yoon!

99
04:42.992 --> 04:44.159
-[overlapping chatter] -[executive 3] Hold on!

100
04:44.243 --> 04:46.829
[Jae-hee sighs] I don't want to. Why should I get on this ride with you?

101
04:46.912 --> 04:48.455
Because I wanna go on it.

102
04:48.539 --> 04:50.332
Then just go on it by yourself.

103
04:50.874 --> 04:52.960
-[annoyed sigh] -[man] Thank you. [chuckles]

104
04:53.961 --> 04:55.421
Let's get on the ride, Ma.

105
04:56.797 --> 04:58.090
Uh…

106
05:01.010 --> 05:02.011
[Yi-jun sighs]

107
05:02.094 --> 05:05.055
If you've caught on, play along with my abuse of authority.

108
05:10.728 --> 05:12.354
I wasn't expecting this.

109
05:13.272 --> 05:15.274
He could have just told me what was going on.

110
05:15.357 --> 05:19.153
[gentle music playing]

111
05:23.282 --> 05:24.199
[inhales]

112
05:24.283 --> 05:26.952
During the interview, didn't you say that…

113
05:27.911 --> 05:29.830
you witnessed your squad mate's death?

114
05:29.913 --> 05:31.290
[inhales] Was that his son?

115
05:31.373 --> 05:33.417
I don't want to discuss personal matters, sir.

116
05:33.917 --> 05:35.335
I stopped working for you, you know.

117
05:36.628 --> 05:37.504
Ah.

118
05:38.005 --> 05:39.173
And the rumor has it

119
05:39.256 --> 05:41.175
that you went straight to work for Lee Si-a.

120
05:41.258 --> 05:42.926
Well, the rumor is wrong.

121
05:44.261 --> 05:46.597
I know. I know she was lying.

122
05:48.182 --> 05:50.768
I knew you were not so shameless as to go and work for her.

123
05:51.769 --> 05:53.520
I used that as an excuse

124
05:54.229 --> 05:55.689
to come here to stop you.

125
05:56.565 --> 05:58.567
So what I'm trying to get at is…

126
05:58.984 --> 06:02.279
I bet you wanted to say that I should do better, right?

127
06:03.739 --> 06:04.740
I'm sorry

128
06:05.491 --> 06:06.992
for getting so angry.

129
06:07.076 --> 06:09.661
[gentle music playing]

130
06:11.038 --> 06:14.208
It was the first time… I experienced something like that.

131
06:14.875 --> 06:16.335
You're the first one

132
06:16.794 --> 06:19.088
to ever get this far into my world. Know what I mean?

133
06:20.756 --> 06:23.008
Still, you didn't have to lash out at me like that.

134
06:23.092 --> 06:25.511
You knew I was only worried for your safety.

135
06:25.594 --> 06:27.596
What's wrong with you? Am I a joke to you?

136
06:27.679 --> 06:30.015
Well, you're the most disobedient subordinate

137
06:30.099 --> 06:31.433
that's worked for me,

138
06:31.517 --> 06:33.227
-but you're not a joke. -[sighs]

139
06:36.939 --> 06:37.940
I mean…

140
06:39.274 --> 06:40.776
I decided to accept it.

141
06:42.402 --> 06:43.654
Kang Jae-hee.

142
06:46.240 --> 06:47.574
I wanted to say…

143
06:48.367 --> 06:49.326
I…

144
06:50.077 --> 06:50.911
like…

145
06:52.079 --> 06:53.205
really need you.

146
06:54.289 --> 06:55.707
I think that's what it is.

147
07:05.300 --> 07:07.219
You all thinking what I'm thinking?

148
07:07.302 --> 07:08.512
Surprise inspection.

149
07:11.306 --> 07:14.810
Let's show them that operations are running smoothly with no hitches.

150
07:14.893 --> 07:15.811
Yeah.

151
07:16.186 --> 07:19.064
What then? Shall we play it by the book?

152
07:20.440 --> 07:22.442
[whimsical orchestral music playing]

153
07:29.158 --> 07:31.201
WE LOVE YOU, MANAGING DIRECTOR YOON

154
07:31.285 --> 07:33.328
-WELCOME TO FANTASY LAND -EMPLOYEES OF FANTASY LAND-

155
07:33.412 --> 07:35.831
[upbeat bright music playing]

156
07:36.748 --> 07:39.209
[sighs] What the hell are they doing?

157
07:40.919 --> 07:41.837
Uh…

158
07:43.255 --> 07:44.256
[man] Mother, look at that.

159
07:44.339 --> 07:47.217
-[man's mom gasps in awe] -[man chuckles]

160
07:47.301 --> 07:48.510
[man's mom] Pretty, huh?

161
07:51.930 --> 07:53.765
So you've come running to say you need me.

162
07:53.849 --> 07:55.350
Do you think I have no pride?

163
07:55.434 --> 07:58.854
Keep your pride and let me keep you. I'll set the stage for you.

164
07:59.771 --> 08:00.981
Would you like a raise?

165
08:01.064 --> 08:03.025
There you go, flexing your money.

166
08:03.108 --> 08:04.193
Forget about the money…

167
08:05.986 --> 08:07.446
and just let me hit you for me.

168
08:11.200 --> 08:14.203
Huh, that proves I was right. You're all talk.

169
08:14.578 --> 08:15.662
I knew it.

170
08:19.374 --> 08:22.419
Get it over with. You won't get this opportunity again.

171
08:24.171 --> 08:28.675
[scoffs] If you're thinking of sending me your medical bills or suing me later…

172
08:28.759 --> 08:30.177
I won't do that.

173
08:31.386 --> 08:32.387
But…

174
08:32.471 --> 08:34.514
if you're gonna go all out with your punches,

175
08:34.598 --> 08:35.724
call the ambulance first.

176
08:35.807 --> 08:39.061
How about you close your eyes and clench your teeth real hard?

177
08:39.144 --> 08:40.270
Okay.

178
08:40.354 --> 08:43.690
[breathes deeply]

179
08:44.107 --> 08:45.025
[clears throat]

180
08:49.613 --> 08:50.948
-[Jae-hee grunts] -[groans]

181
08:51.031 --> 08:51.949
[groans]

182
08:52.032 --> 08:54.159
Oh, come on. All I did was flick your forehead.

183
08:54.243 --> 08:56.203
I went really easy on you.

184
08:56.703 --> 08:58.413
[groaning]

185
08:58.497 --> 09:00.123
Let me see, let me see.

186
09:00.207 --> 09:01.500
[Yi-jun] Right here.

187
09:02.084 --> 09:03.669
You sure that wasn't a rock?

188
09:04.378 --> 09:05.796
[Jae-hee] Just my finger.

189
09:05.879 --> 09:07.714
-[Yi-jun] Felt like a rock! -[Jae-hee] You let me hit you!

190
09:07.798 --> 09:08.632
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

191
09:08.715 --> 09:09.549
EPISODE 7

192
09:09.633 --> 09:11.677
[Si-hyun sighs] I just strained my back.

193
09:11.760 --> 09:14.012
When I came here with Jun, you had our seats ready.

194
09:14.096 --> 09:16.014
But now I guess I have to get my own chair.

195
09:16.098 --> 09:17.391
Ugh. Sheesh.

196
09:17.474 --> 09:18.600
[Captain Park] She had no idea.

197
09:19.059 --> 09:22.187
Ms. Lee had no idea he would come here, did she?

198
09:22.271 --> 09:23.605
How did he know she was here?

199
09:23.689 --> 09:25.983
[dramatic music sting]

200
09:26.066 --> 09:27.985
-Superintendent Ma? -[shushes]

201
09:29.987 --> 09:31.530
[Captain Park sighs]

202
09:33.115 --> 09:34.783
We already asked her in advance

203
09:34.866 --> 09:36.410
whether she would like an attorney present.

204
09:36.493 --> 09:37.327
She said no.

205
09:37.411 --> 09:38.287
Is that so?

206
09:38.370 --> 09:39.454
[Si-hyun] Hmm.

207
09:40.289 --> 09:41.915
Hey, uh, Ms. Lee.

208
09:42.499 --> 09:45.711
The police have the primary authority to close the investigation.

209
09:46.295 --> 09:48.797
That means your response during the investigation stage

210
09:48.880 --> 09:50.757
is very important.

211
09:50.841 --> 09:52.718
So I highly recommend that you

212
09:52.801 --> 09:55.804
exercise your right to an attorney to defend yourself. Do you agree?

213
09:57.973 --> 09:59.725
[tense music playing]

214
09:59.808 --> 10:03.061
Who the hell does he think he is, showing up out of the blue like that?

215
10:03.145 --> 10:05.355
He's trying to control what we see.

216
10:06.231 --> 10:07.441
He's playing hardball.

217
10:10.319 --> 10:11.778
How did your last call with her go?

218
10:13.613 --> 10:15.282
It was just a routine check-in call.

219
10:15.824 --> 10:17.909
[papers rustling]

220
10:17.993 --> 10:21.413
You received some photos from Ms. Han soon after that call. Is that correct?

221
10:22.456 --> 10:24.916
-[papers rustling] -Why did you delete them?

222
10:27.252 --> 10:29.296
Did you request these files from Ms. Han first?

223
10:29.379 --> 10:30.714
ATTACHED PHOTO

224
10:31.882 --> 10:33.008
Answer the question.

225
10:38.472 --> 10:41.975
[Si-hyun] They're trying to determine whether the elements of crime are met.

226
10:42.059 --> 10:43.602
If you didn't request them, say so.

227
10:48.148 --> 10:50.525
I didn't request them, Detective.

228
10:51.151 --> 10:53.111
[papers rustling]

229
10:53.195 --> 10:54.446
[Captain Park sighs]

230
11:03.955 --> 11:05.540
[Yi-jun] Ms. Han sent her the files?

231
11:05.624 --> 11:07.167
So that's how they were leaked.

232
11:07.250 --> 11:08.585
And Ms. Lee?

233
11:09.294 --> 11:10.337
She's staying quiet for now.

234
11:10.420 --> 11:11.838
I'll try to meet with her.

235
11:11.922 --> 11:12.798
That's dangerous.

236
11:13.298 --> 11:14.174
[sighs]

237
11:14.591 --> 11:16.927
Hey, you're the one who's worried someone could get hurt.

238
11:17.010 --> 11:20.305
We have to know whether seeing the files gave Ms. Lee a sword or a shield at least.

239
11:20.972 --> 11:22.307
We have to be prepared.

240
11:24.476 --> 11:26.895
Look, I gotta know what happened to your forehead, huh?

241
11:28.355 --> 11:30.023
Was it a wasp or a mosquito?

242
11:31.441 --> 11:32.359
Is that bad?

243
11:34.319 --> 11:35.779
For argument's sake…

244
11:36.196 --> 11:38.156
let's say Ms. Han sent the files along.

245
11:38.240 --> 11:40.867
Why was Yoon Yi-jun going over them in the first place?

246
11:40.951 --> 11:44.538
I mean, you gotta admit, he doesn't exactly look like a hero.

247
11:44.621 --> 11:46.873
Actually, if you look kind of closely, he does.

248
11:46.957 --> 11:48.125
He's got a kind heart.

249
11:48.208 --> 11:50.001
What? Are you feeling all right?

250
11:50.085 --> 11:51.044
Get a grip.

251
11:52.045 --> 11:54.297
Ugh, what's important here is that Mr. Yoon is in

252
11:54.381 --> 11:55.799
-a lot of danger because of all of this. -[scoffs]

253
11:55.882 --> 11:58.969
If these records are legit, we had the chandelier, the weed killer.

254
11:59.052 --> 12:00.595
What's next on the list?

255
12:00.679 --> 12:01.680
"Mr. Yoon"?

256
12:02.264 --> 12:03.932
-I'm gonna have to stop you right there. -[gasps]

257
12:04.224 --> 12:05.934
You think you're a real personal secretary?

258
12:06.017 --> 12:07.686
-Yoon Yi-jun, Yoon Yi-jun. -That's right.

259
12:07.769 --> 12:08.812
[phone buzzes]

260
12:11.273 --> 12:12.482
FANTASY LAND PR TEAM

261
12:17.404 --> 12:18.822
I thought you lost it and quit.

262
12:18.905 --> 12:20.240
Uh…

263
12:20.323 --> 12:22.701
Didn't you say begging for your job back would be humiliating?

264
12:22.784 --> 12:25.370
Then why did you take a photo looking like best buds?

265
12:25.745 --> 12:27.414
I took Jin-hyung to a theme park

266
12:27.497 --> 12:29.124
-because it was his birthday. -[Wan-gu] Hmm.

267
12:29.207 --> 12:30.250
How did this happen?

268
12:32.502 --> 12:34.880
Uh, well, it just kinda…

269
12:37.299 --> 12:38.383
[Jae-hee] Does it hurt a lot?

270
12:38.758 --> 12:40.552
[Yi-jun] You hit me right on the corner.

271
12:41.803 --> 12:43.513
[whispers] This is where it hurts the most.

272
12:44.598 --> 12:46.099
Well, that's a decent bruise.

273
12:46.808 --> 12:48.185
You'll be fine tomorrow.

274
12:48.810 --> 12:51.229
I only applied 10% of my pent-up frustrations.

275
12:51.563 --> 12:53.148
[whispers] I considered your public image.

276
12:54.191 --> 12:55.859
That's so nice of you.

277
12:56.735 --> 12:57.736
Anyway,

278
12:58.403 --> 12:59.446
now that that's settled,

279
12:59.529 --> 13:02.324
come into work as usual, Mr. Special Forces.

280
13:02.407 --> 13:03.241
Yep.

281
13:03.325 --> 13:04.910
[Yi-jun] Tch.

282
13:05.410 --> 13:08.246
Now that our labor dispute has been amicably resolved,

283
13:08.330 --> 13:09.498
abuse your power once again.

284
13:10.165 --> 13:13.001
[man] Mom, let's take a photo here before we go.

285
13:13.084 --> 13:14.252
Give me a smile.

286
13:15.545 --> 13:17.797
[man's mom] Oh, no. What are you taking pictures for?

287
13:17.881 --> 13:18.798
-It's so embarrassing. -[man] Oh, Mom.

288
13:18.882 --> 13:19.883
You look so pretty today. Give me a smile.

289
13:19.966 --> 13:21.092
-[clears throat] -[laughter]

290
13:21.176 --> 13:22.552
-Come here. -[executive 2] Yes, sir.

291
13:23.762 --> 13:24.721
[man] Oh, are you seriously camera shy?

292
13:24.804 --> 13:27.224
Apparently, this is the hottest attraction in Fantasy Land.

293
13:27.307 --> 13:28.225
Is that right?

294
13:28.308 --> 13:29.976
-Yes, that's correct, sir. -Right you are, sir.

295
13:30.060 --> 13:31.937
It's so dark, I can barely see it.

296
13:32.020 --> 13:33.355
-Oh, we should get the lights. -Oh.

297
13:33.438 --> 13:34.481
-Uh, the lights. -Lights, lights. Turn on the lights.

298
13:34.564 --> 13:36.316
-[executive 1] Get the lights on. -Wow.

299
13:36.399 --> 13:39.736
[dreamy, whimsical music playing]

300
13:39.819 --> 13:41.571
-[man] Wow. Look at that. -Whoa…

301
13:41.655 --> 13:43.490
-Oh, did you see that? -[man] It's so pretty.

302
13:43.907 --> 13:44.991
-[chuckles] -[man's mom] Oh!

303
13:45.075 --> 13:46.743
-It's so pretty. I love it. -How pretty.

304
13:46.826 --> 13:48.370
Would you like to try going on the ride, sir?

305
13:48.453 --> 13:49.788
Not this time.

306
13:53.833 --> 13:54.834
Okay, well…

307
13:55.460 --> 13:57.379
a personal inspection couldn't hurt.

308
13:59.881 --> 14:00.924
Am I also getting on?

309
14:01.007 --> 14:02.384
Do you want me to ride it myself?

310
14:02.467 --> 14:03.843
I've been on it a lot today.

311
14:04.177 --> 14:06.221
-Hmm. -Hmm.

312
14:06.304 --> 14:07.430
[chuckles softly]

313
14:07.514 --> 14:09.349
[executive 1] Okay, I'm taking the photo now.

314
14:09.432 --> 14:11.268
One, two, three.

315
14:11.351 --> 14:12.644
-[soft yelp] -[camera shutter clicks]

316
14:12.727 --> 14:14.229
[camera shutter clicking]

317
14:23.572 --> 14:25.240
[Yi-jun] I used that as an excuse

318
14:25.824 --> 14:27.284
to come here to stop you.

319
14:27.576 --> 14:30.870
Why would he say something like that when he's engaged to someone?

320
14:30.954 --> 14:31.830
I wanted to say…

321
14:32.747 --> 14:34.165
I really need you.

322
14:34.708 --> 14:37.085
Ugh, all he's done is make me feel really weird.

323
14:37.919 --> 14:38.837
[sighs]

324
14:40.213 --> 14:41.506
[Si-hyun] Wow.

325
14:41.590 --> 14:43.550
He did that to your forehead? Does it hurt?

326
14:43.633 --> 14:44.926
-Hurts a lot. -[pops]

327
14:45.010 --> 14:46.720
-[Yi-jun groans] -[exclaims]

328
14:46.803 --> 14:49.264
He put a whole frigging mountain on your forehead, man.

329
14:49.347 --> 14:51.474
From now on, I'll treat him with a little more respect.

330
14:51.558 --> 14:53.435
Kang Jae-hee's super strong.

331
14:53.852 --> 14:55.687
Whoa, you sound quite proud of him.

332
14:55.770 --> 14:57.439
Whatever happened to going back to normal?

333
14:57.522 --> 14:58.940
Couldn't do it.

334
14:59.482 --> 15:02.360
And before I knew it, I was begging him not to go.

335
15:02.444 --> 15:03.486
Oh…

336
15:04.696 --> 15:05.530
Can you see it?

337
15:05.614 --> 15:06.615
Totally.

338
15:06.698 --> 15:07.532
Really?

339
15:07.616 --> 15:09.200
Hey, are you gonna be all right?

340
15:09.284 --> 15:10.410
No, I don't think so.

341
15:11.077 --> 15:12.162
It hurts so much.

342
15:12.245 --> 15:14.289
[sighs] I don't mean that thing.

343
15:14.372 --> 15:16.750
The chairman, the board, your wedding, the slush fund…

344
15:16.833 --> 15:17.917
Even I find it suffocating,

345
15:18.001 --> 15:20.837
and you're still going on about your forehead? Huh?

346
15:23.173 --> 15:24.341
Anyway…

347
15:25.967 --> 15:28.720
I should get to have Kang Jae-hee by my side at the least.

348
15:29.262 --> 15:32.098
Of the countless things that are happening to me that aren't quite all right…

349
15:32.182 --> 15:33.099
[inhales]

350
15:33.183 --> 15:35.101
…he's the only thing that is all right.

351
15:36.603 --> 15:38.605
Besides, he won't ever find out about it.

352
15:38.688 --> 15:39.898
Are you stupid?

353
15:40.815 --> 15:42.317
Are you telling me you have a crush on a guy?

354
15:42.400 --> 15:44.694
Didn't you say that humans should love each other?

355
15:44.778 --> 15:46.613
-My focus wasn't on the man part. -[groans]

356
15:46.696 --> 15:48.323
It was on you having a crush.

357
15:49.574 --> 15:51.242
What's wrong with feeling that way?

358
15:51.326 --> 15:53.536
You only say that 'cause you've never experienced it.

359
15:53.620 --> 15:56.164
Buddy, I don't wanna sound cliché, but…

360
15:56.247 --> 15:57.332
as Homo sapiens,

361
15:57.415 --> 15:59.542
there's a few things that we really can't hide.

362
16:00.377 --> 16:02.545
And what you're planning on doing is one of them.

363
16:02.629 --> 16:03.880
We can't hide a crush.

364
16:04.506 --> 16:06.424
It's bound to show one way or another,

365
16:06.925 --> 16:09.094
-just like your forehead, you know? -[soft pensive music playing]

366
16:09.844 --> 16:10.929
[sighs softly]

367
16:15.850 --> 16:17.852
-[driver] Whoa, what's going on? -[bus chuffs]

368
16:20.563 --> 16:21.940
[air hissing]

369
16:22.023 --> 16:22.857
[sighs]

370
16:23.650 --> 16:25.110
[driver] I'm sorry, everyone.

371
16:25.193 --> 16:26.528
Looks like the bus broke down.

372
16:26.611 --> 16:28.571
I'm afraid you'll have to get a different one.

373
16:29.114 --> 16:30.115
Oh, man.

374
16:31.074 --> 16:32.492
Really sorry, guys.

375
16:32.575 --> 16:34.327
-[driver] Yes. -Sir, good morning.

376
16:35.412 --> 16:36.621
[Yi-jun] Where are you?

377
16:37.247 --> 16:38.164
The bus did what?

378
16:38.707 --> 16:40.291
Did it crash? Are you hurt?

379
16:40.375 --> 16:41.918
Are you wounded? Are you gonna die?

380
16:42.001 --> 16:43.169
Do you need a chopper?

381
16:43.878 --> 16:44.879
Oh.

382
16:45.714 --> 16:46.965
It broke down.

383
16:47.799 --> 16:48.883
I see.

384
16:49.676 --> 16:53.096
Please take your time and come here carefully. Understood?

385
16:56.891 --> 16:58.059
"Carefully"?

386
16:59.018 --> 17:00.645
[running steps approaching]

387
17:01.771 --> 17:03.857
[Jae-hee panting]

388
17:04.274 --> 17:05.483
[Jae-hee] Oh, sir!

389
17:06.651 --> 17:07.736
I'm sorry I'm late, sir.

390
17:08.903 --> 17:10.822
I had to run here because the bus broke down.

391
17:11.281 --> 17:12.449
So that's why I'm late.

392
17:12.532 --> 17:13.825
[panting]

393
17:13.908 --> 17:16.202
Uh, may I have a drink of water?

394
17:22.292 --> 17:23.418
Drink up.

395
17:23.501 --> 17:25.712
Whoa. Uh, thank you, sir.

396
17:27.547 --> 17:28.882
Just call me next time.

397
17:28.965 --> 17:29.966
So I don't worry about you.

398
17:30.049 --> 17:31.718
[gags, groans]

399
17:33.470 --> 17:34.512
You okay?

400
17:35.555 --> 17:36.389
Uh…

401
17:36.890 --> 17:37.724
Drink up.

402
17:38.600 --> 17:40.685
It's all right. I'm all good, sir.

403
17:40.769 --> 17:42.687
I wouldn't dare drink your drink.

404
17:43.229 --> 17:45.815
Tell me, are you turning it down because it's my drink,

405
17:46.232 --> 17:47.942
or is it because you think it has a bitter taste?

406
17:49.319 --> 17:50.487
Don't be a child.

407
17:50.904 --> 17:52.238
It's good for you. Drink up.

408
17:53.156 --> 17:54.073
Drink it.

409
17:54.157 --> 17:54.991
Okay.

410
17:55.700 --> 17:57.368
[clears throat] Thank you, sir.

411
17:59.579 --> 18:01.206
[sniffs, puffs]

412
18:01.289 --> 18:02.290
[sucks teeth]

413
18:06.586 --> 18:09.130
Ugh, it's bitter. [coughs]

414
18:09.214 --> 18:10.298
[stifled chuckle]

415
18:15.220 --> 18:16.513
Hey, what gives?

416
18:16.596 --> 18:18.848
You don't get to laugh when someone else is in pain.

417
18:19.265 --> 18:20.099
So why'd you laugh?

418
18:20.183 --> 18:21.226
It was cute.

419
18:21.309 --> 18:22.227
[splutters]

420
18:22.310 --> 18:23.353
Stop saying things like that.

421
18:23.853 --> 18:25.355
What's wrong with calling something "cute"?

422
18:26.064 --> 18:27.440
Ah…

423
18:28.233 --> 18:29.567
Is it 'cause you're a guy?

424
18:30.151 --> 18:33.071
Don't tell me you'd rather hear you're "cool" instead of "cute."

425
18:33.154 --> 18:35.573
No. Well, not… not exactly.

426
18:36.366 --> 18:37.450
Could you just stop saying it?

427
18:37.534 --> 18:38.785
I'll do what I want.

428
18:39.536 --> 18:41.538
Do I need your permission to say something's cute

429
18:41.621 --> 18:42.539
when I think it's cute?

430
18:42.622 --> 18:44.457
Ugh, stop! Stop teasing me, sir. Please!

431
18:46.626 --> 18:47.961
Oh, good morning.

432
18:51.297 --> 18:52.131
[Si-hyun] What's this?

433
18:52.215 --> 18:53.925
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

434
18:55.385 --> 18:56.386
What's going on?

435
18:57.095 --> 18:58.847
[employee 1] "Lee Hye-jung, the Taekang Goddess,

436
18:58.930 --> 19:00.640
and Kim Si-hyun, the Taekang Idol.

437
19:00.723 --> 19:03.017
At first, these two stars weren't an item at all.

438
19:03.893 --> 19:06.563
However, Taespatch has recently spotted them

439
19:06.646 --> 19:09.107
visiting each other's homes and openly dating,"

440
19:09.190 --> 19:10.608
and yada, yada, yada. Anyway…

441
19:11.359 --> 19:13.820
In conclusion, they are no longer just colleagues.

442
19:13.903 --> 19:16.030
They are a couple in love, aren't they?

443
19:16.114 --> 19:17.991
Mr. Kim, give us a statement.

444
19:18.408 --> 19:19.534
Are these rumors true?

445
19:20.493 --> 19:21.870
I guess they're half true.

446
19:21.953 --> 19:23.079
Oh, there's that lawyer-speak.

447
19:23.162 --> 19:24.706
[employee 2] Ugh, is it a yes or a no?

448
19:24.789 --> 19:26.833
Well, we went on a few dates.

449
19:26.916 --> 19:27.750
Uh…

450
19:28.376 --> 19:29.294
but I got dumped.

451
19:29.377 --> 19:30.879
[employee 1] Oh, my, my, my, my, my.

452
19:30.962 --> 19:33.965
Welcome, Mr. Kim, to the Lee Hye-jung Rejects' Alliance.

453
19:34.340 --> 19:36.676
-Please don't hesitate to join us. -[chuckles]

454
19:37.802 --> 19:39.304
Okay, settle down.

455
19:39.888 --> 19:44.517
Uh, so, uh, I did actually date her, so where does that put me in the ranks?

456
19:44.601 --> 19:46.185
Has anyone dated her?

457
19:46.269 --> 19:47.478
Do let me know.

458
19:49.606 --> 19:51.065
[employee 1] You're still welcome regardless.

459
19:52.066 --> 19:53.610
[employee 1 chuckles]

460
19:53.693 --> 19:55.737
So Ms. L dumped Mr. K?

461
19:56.154 --> 19:57.739
It says Mr. Kim admitted it.

462
19:58.406 --> 19:59.324
[tray clatters]

463
19:59.741 --> 20:01.034
I guess that's my cue.

464
20:01.743 --> 20:04.120
Mm. I should get going.

465
20:12.378 --> 20:14.130
[exhales deeply]

466
20:15.590 --> 20:17.508
I'm not here to talk about personal matters.

467
20:19.177 --> 20:21.137
Would you be open to meeting up with Mr. Yoon Yi-jun?

468
20:22.013 --> 20:24.057
I talked him out of coming to see you himself.

469
20:25.183 --> 20:27.018
Do what you want. We're not trying to force you.

470
20:27.977 --> 20:28.978
Why, though?

471
20:31.189 --> 20:33.316
You're a client, and I'm your lawyer.

472
20:33.399 --> 20:34.943
I'm just doing my job. That's why.

473
20:39.280 --> 20:41.407
How did you know I'd be at the police station?

474
20:42.033 --> 20:43.117
The police got in touch.

475
20:44.577 --> 20:45.745
So everyone's in on it.

476
20:49.082 --> 20:49.999
[utensils clatter]

477
20:52.043 --> 20:53.795
In on it? You know, that hurts my pride a little.

478
20:55.296 --> 20:57.715
I'll have you know I'm rather partial to seeking justice.

479
20:58.841 --> 21:00.885
This isn't the time to be splitting hairs.

480
21:01.678 --> 21:03.262
But you know that better than I do.

481
21:04.013 --> 21:06.432
You think I was the only one that the cops called?

482
21:07.600 --> 21:10.687
I'm sure whoever did Ms. Han in also got a call to balance things out.

483
21:11.396 --> 21:14.148
And if the cops are even closer with them than they are with us,

484
21:14.232 --> 21:15.817
then I bet they know a lot more than we do.

485
21:17.360 --> 21:19.112
All your cards are on the table now.

486
21:19.195 --> 21:20.905
If you won't talk to the police,

487
21:20.989 --> 21:24.325
then you should at least talk to your lawyer so he can help.

488
21:25.994 --> 21:27.912
Just don't hit me in the back of the head again.

489
21:31.499 --> 21:32.542
[grunts]

490
21:32.625 --> 21:33.543
You looking at my head?

491
21:35.545 --> 21:38.464
Ugh, I can't even sit in front of you 'cause I'm afraid.

492
21:39.298 --> 21:41.467
I'm only gonna sit next to you from now on.

493
21:45.013 --> 21:49.517
BROKEN/UNDER REPAIRS

494
22:03.281 --> 22:04.198
[inhales]

495
22:04.282 --> 22:06.200
Stop overreacting and make space.

496
22:07.243 --> 22:08.077
Oh…

497
22:12.707 --> 22:13.583
[inhales]

498
22:17.045 --> 22:17.920
[elevator chimes]

499
22:22.008 --> 22:23.718
[breathes nervously]

500
22:33.936 --> 22:35.563
[Jae-hee's mom] They're totally having a fling.

501
22:36.397 --> 22:38.399
[neighbor 1] The flower shop and the chicken place?

502
22:38.483 --> 22:40.651
Don't be ridiculous. Those two are always fighting!

503
22:40.735 --> 22:42.487
Fights, flings.

504
22:42.570 --> 22:44.697
Switch out a few letters, and you have a love affair.

505
22:44.781 --> 22:48.076
Affection forged by hate is the most powerful of them all.

506
22:48.159 --> 22:49.494
-Fighting got them together. -Uh-huh.

507
22:49.577 --> 22:51.329
I guess you don't have to worry about that.

508
22:51.788 --> 22:52.622
No?

509
22:52.705 --> 22:55.041
-[neighbor 2] Because he's so handsome. -[door opens]

510
22:55.792 --> 22:59.212
[mellow romantic music playing]

511
23:09.472 --> 23:11.224
[both gasp in slow motion]

512
23:14.185 --> 23:15.812
[gasps in slow motion]

513
23:21.150 --> 23:24.237
[chuckles softly] A face like that could win anyone's heart.

514
23:24.737 --> 23:27.240
[sighs] That was a long time ago.

515
23:27.323 --> 23:28.825
He's just some old guy now.

516
23:28.908 --> 23:31.369
Hey, do you still livestream with a mask on?

517
23:32.078 --> 23:33.704
Do you? Does it pay well?

518
23:33.788 --> 23:36.249
Ma'am, it pays okay.

519
23:36.332 --> 23:39.127
So long as you like and subscribe…

520
23:39.877 --> 23:40.920
I'll love you.

521
23:41.003 --> 23:42.839
-[both squeal, chuckle] -Okay, okay.

522
23:42.922 --> 23:44.632
-I'll like, comment, and subscribe. -[chuckles]

523
23:44.715 --> 23:46.092
[neighbors chuckling]

524
23:46.175 --> 23:48.136
Who do you think you are, Chow Yun-fat?

525
23:49.637 --> 23:51.305
A job satisfaction survey?

526
23:51.389 --> 23:54.851
Uh-huh. I said you'd go first since I have to help prepare an event,

527
23:54.934 --> 23:55.768
so go on.

528
23:55.852 --> 23:57.228
[Jae-hee] Right. I see.

529
23:57.311 --> 23:59.480
But isn't there something I can help you with?

530
23:59.564 --> 24:00.982
You've been working overtime.

531
24:01.065 --> 24:02.191
All right.

532
24:02.275 --> 24:05.111
I see you prepared me a yawn-inducing opening speech.

533
24:06.696 --> 24:07.655
Mr. Kwon.

534
24:09.031 --> 24:10.074
Show me the other one.

535
24:14.954 --> 24:16.414
What? Aren't you leaving?

536
24:16.873 --> 24:19.083
I'm leaving. I'll be right back, sir.

537
24:21.711 --> 24:25.131
Don't give him anything to do for a while. I need him for something else.

538
24:25.214 --> 24:27.800
-I must have been Kongjwi in my past life. -[door opens, closes]

539
24:27.884 --> 24:29.343
The stepmother only sides with Patjwi.

540
24:29.427 --> 24:31.304
[enunciating] Want me to…

541
24:31.929 --> 24:33.723
take his side? Really?

542
24:34.765 --> 24:37.602
Should I commit to being an evil stepmother?

543
24:40.730 --> 24:43.107
JOB SATISFACTION SURVEY

544
24:48.070 --> 24:49.614
How do you manage your job stress?

545
24:49.697 --> 24:50.740
I basically work out.

546
24:50.823 --> 24:52.783
I've been doing taekwondo, jujitsu,

547
24:52.867 --> 24:55.036
and lately, I've developed an interest in boxing.

548
24:55.119 --> 24:57.455
But when I don't have enough time to work out,

549
24:57.538 --> 24:59.373
I go outside to have a run.

550
24:59.457 --> 25:00.541
I like the Han River.

551
25:01.000 --> 25:03.794
When I'm running at night, so I race against the cruise ships there.

552
25:03.878 --> 25:05.838
Kind of like, uh, how they made a person

553
25:05.922 --> 25:08.549
race against a subway train on TV a long time ago.

554
25:09.008 --> 25:11.427
Like that. That's what I do.

555
25:13.763 --> 25:15.681
RELATIONSHIP WITH BOSS AND COLLEAGUES

556
25:15.765 --> 25:18.434
HOW SATISFIED ARE YOU WITH YOUR BOSS?

557
25:19.101 --> 25:20.019
[inhales]

558
25:21.771 --> 25:23.189
Just to make sure…

559
25:24.523 --> 25:25.691
this survey

560
25:25.775 --> 25:27.860
is completely anonymous, right?

561
25:30.071 --> 25:31.155
As of late…

562
25:32.573 --> 25:33.616
my boss has, uh,

563
25:34.367 --> 25:35.618
been acting really weird.

564
25:36.244 --> 25:37.078
[camera shutter clicks]

565
25:40.998 --> 25:42.792
[Jae-hee] The expressions he makes…

566
25:43.459 --> 25:44.293
[stifled chuckle]

567
25:44.377 --> 25:46.087
-So I don't worry about you. -[gulps, gags]

568
25:46.170 --> 25:48.798
The way he talks, and even the way he's been acting.

569
25:50.466 --> 25:51.592
Even his face.

570
25:53.177 --> 25:54.929
But your anonymous friend

571
25:55.012 --> 25:57.431
is beginning to act even weirder than before?

572
25:58.432 --> 26:00.935
Every time they look at their boss who's acting weird,

573
26:01.352 --> 26:04.897
they're all confused, and their heart keeps fluttering?

574
26:05.314 --> 26:06.148
Yeah.

575
26:06.649 --> 26:07.650
Is the boss good-looking?

576
26:09.068 --> 26:10.403
Well, kinda.

577
26:10.486 --> 26:11.320
Are they rich?

578
26:11.404 --> 26:13.281
Oof, I'd be lying if I said they weren't.

579
26:13.906 --> 26:16.075
[grunts] There's your answer.

580
26:16.742 --> 26:19.370
Hey, this is a no-brainer. What's there to even think about?

581
26:21.122 --> 26:23.165
That anonymous secretary friend of yours…

582
26:23.249 --> 26:24.166
Mm.

583
26:24.250 --> 26:25.584
…and their boss,

584
26:26.127 --> 26:26.961
they're, um…

585
26:27.628 --> 26:28.462
"Um"?

586
26:29.463 --> 26:31.382
…seeing which one of them should resign first.

587
26:31.465 --> 26:32.300
Playing chicken.

588
26:32.383 --> 26:33.676
One has to leave the company, right?

589
26:33.759 --> 26:36.470
So their hearts keep skipping a beat like this, you know? Huh?

590
26:37.096 --> 26:38.222
-Here, take this. -Huh?

591
26:38.306 --> 26:39.640
It's time to go home.

592
26:39.724 --> 26:40.975
Get out of here.

593
26:41.058 --> 26:42.101
That didn't help.

594
26:42.601 --> 26:44.270
-All right, fine. -[can thuds]

595
26:44.353 --> 26:45.646
Just tell your friend

596
26:46.397 --> 26:47.898
they should ask their boss in person.

597
26:50.192 --> 26:53.863
-[light music playing] -[rattling]

598
26:54.322 --> 26:55.156
[sighs]

599
26:55.239 --> 26:57.241
[Jae-hee's dad] I mean, they're not mind readers, are they?

600
26:57.325 --> 27:00.453
They need to decide how they feel and take action, or they'll never know.

601
27:00.536 --> 27:02.455
Good grief, you're impossible. Sheesh.

602
27:06.292 --> 27:07.918
[inhales] Hmm.

603
27:08.544 --> 27:10.713
MR. YOON

604
27:10.796 --> 27:11.797
[phone buzzing]

605
27:12.923 --> 27:13.841
Sir, how can I help?

606
27:13.924 --> 27:15.092
Where are you?

607
27:16.010 --> 27:18.429
How is it that you seem to always…

608
27:18.888 --> 27:21.015
The job satisfaction score you gave me…

609
27:21.098 --> 27:22.558
[breathes deeply]

610
27:23.100 --> 27:24.060
Forget it.

611
27:24.602 --> 27:27.188
You've got ten minutes to get over here.

612
27:27.271 --> 27:28.564
[yells angrily] Hurry!

613
27:29.565 --> 27:30.441
[phone beeps]

614
27:30.524 --> 27:32.443
[breathing angrily]

615
27:32.526 --> 27:33.527
Q. HOW SATISFIED ARE YOU WITH YOUR BOSS?

616
27:33.611 --> 27:34.779
He gave me…

617
27:35.529 --> 27:37.114
no score?

618
27:38.491 --> 27:41.035
As a boss, I deserve a failing score. Is that it?

619
27:42.912 --> 27:45.414
[breathing angrily]

620
27:45.498 --> 27:49.335
[light background music playing]

621
27:52.421 --> 27:53.589
Right this way.

622
27:53.672 --> 27:54.507
Thank you.

623
27:58.302 --> 27:59.303
Excuse me.

624
28:01.097 --> 28:03.265
I told you that I would come over to your house.

625
28:03.349 --> 28:04.350
Why are we…

626
28:05.101 --> 28:07.603
[gentle romantic music playing]

627
28:12.400 --> 28:14.110
I happened to have some business here.

628
28:16.946 --> 28:18.072
And they also…

629
28:20.157 --> 28:21.200
sold this to me.

630
28:21.700 --> 28:23.202
They also sell flowers here?

631
28:23.911 --> 28:24.745
Take it.

632
28:24.829 --> 28:26.330
Is… is it for me?

633
28:26.414 --> 28:27.498
[chuckles softly]

634
28:31.001 --> 28:32.002
Take a seat.

635
28:40.219 --> 28:41.637
They really do sell flowers.

636
28:46.016 --> 28:49.270
Okay. Here, order everything you'd like.

637
28:49.353 --> 28:50.396
Everything?

638
28:51.522 --> 28:53.357
[Yi-jun] Ask me to buy you this bar.

639
28:53.441 --> 28:54.275
Scratch that.

640
28:54.358 --> 28:56.485
I could buy this entire building and give it to you.

641
28:57.111 --> 28:58.904
Why are you acting like this all of a sudden?

642
28:58.988 --> 29:00.448
That's the kind of boss I am.

643
29:00.948 --> 29:03.367
I'm a perfect-score kind of boss who's very kind,

644
29:03.826 --> 29:05.744
and very capable, and rich.

645
29:13.502 --> 29:14.503
Sorry, sir, uh…

646
29:14.587 --> 29:15.588
What's up with you?

647
29:16.547 --> 29:17.381
Meaning?

648
29:17.465 --> 29:18.924
Why are you being so nice to me?

649
29:20.801 --> 29:21.635
Am I?

650
29:21.719 --> 29:22.678
Yes.

651
29:23.429 --> 29:24.805
Which brings me to my point.

652
29:24.889 --> 29:26.515
Could it be that you…

653
29:30.978 --> 29:32.354
Do you like me?

654
29:37.026 --> 29:39.236
[breathing shakily]

655
29:48.537 --> 29:50.539
[mouse clicking]

656
29:52.082 --> 29:54.752
[Hye-jung] I was wondering, do you wanna meet up for a bit?

657
29:55.377 --> 29:58.005
I'll come see you. Where are you?

658
29:58.672 --> 30:00.090
[elevator dings]

659
30:02.384 --> 30:05.221
[gentle music playing]

660
30:07.097 --> 30:07.932
[phone beeps]

661
30:09.350 --> 30:11.810
-Going home late? -What are you doing here?

662
30:12.311 --> 30:13.187
It's after hours.

663
30:14.104 --> 30:15.105
Overtime.

664
30:16.607 --> 30:19.944
Why ask when you won't believe me? I know you already know.

665
30:22.530 --> 30:24.114
Why do you keep changing your mind?

666
30:24.198 --> 30:26.325
I suppose it's 'cause that's what you're doing.

667
30:27.326 --> 30:28.410
I can hold a grudge.

668
30:29.245 --> 30:31.830
I kept thinking it over after you dumped me,

669
30:31.914 --> 30:33.415
and that's when it hit me.

670
30:34.708 --> 30:36.877
When I asked you why you approached me on purpose,

671
30:37.795 --> 30:39.004
you said that was enough for you.

672
30:39.088 --> 30:39.922
[inhales]

673
30:40.005 --> 30:43.384
If I were the one who hurt Ms. Han, I wouldn't have asked you that question,

674
30:44.176 --> 30:45.594
and yet, there I was,

675
30:45.678 --> 30:47.763
naively asking you why you did that.

676
30:49.473 --> 30:51.058
You were seeing if I was a bad guy,

677
30:51.141 --> 30:53.811
but when you realized I wasn't, your conscience made you dump me.

678
30:54.770 --> 30:56.772
You know why Ms. Han ended up dead,

679
30:56.855 --> 30:58.857
but you have no idea who did it yet.

680
30:59.525 --> 31:02.069
So that's made you too scared to trust anyone.

681
31:05.406 --> 31:06.240
Don't be scared.

682
31:07.575 --> 31:09.076
I'll play whatever role you like.

683
31:09.159 --> 31:10.119
I can be your lawyer,

684
31:10.202 --> 31:11.829
or I can be your ex.

685
31:12.663 --> 31:13.581
Whatever you need.

686
31:18.711 --> 31:21.797
[gentle music playing]

687
31:27.761 --> 31:29.763
[breathes nervously]

688
31:31.599 --> 31:32.683
Do you have…

689
31:34.310 --> 31:36.645
any idea what you're asking right now?

690
31:37.021 --> 31:37.855
Yeah.

691
31:40.649 --> 31:42.985
You're someone who dislikes most things

692
31:43.068 --> 31:45.154
and only really likes a few things,

693
31:46.530 --> 31:50.034
but then again, when you like a thing, you make a grand display of it.

694
31:51.619 --> 31:55.289
Uh, like with your cat or your action figures.

695
31:56.248 --> 32:01.754
I figured I might… be on that level, I suppose. [chuckles softly]

696
32:03.714 --> 32:04.715
Of course.

697
32:06.175 --> 32:09.845
I guess that would be the best conclusion you would reach in this circumstance.

698
32:11.430 --> 32:12.348
You…

699
32:13.015 --> 32:14.600
are not on that level.

700
32:15.684 --> 32:17.227
Mm. I suppose not.

701
32:17.311 --> 32:19.313
[mutters] Got my hopes up for nothing.

702
32:19.396 --> 32:20.648
[phone buzzing]

703
32:22.941 --> 32:24.610
Uh, I have to get this. I'll be back.

704
32:29.990 --> 32:32.993
[gentle music playing]

705
32:40.918 --> 32:41.877
You're…

706
32:43.087 --> 32:45.297
on a much higher level than that.

707
32:48.133 --> 32:50.803
[Yi-jun] That's why… I need to have you around.

708
32:51.303 --> 32:52.388
Yes, I understand.

709
32:53.305 --> 32:54.515
-[sighs] -[phone beeps]

710
32:55.808 --> 32:56.892
Sorry, sir.

711
32:56.975 --> 32:58.602
I really think you should take a look at your phone.

712
33:02.231 --> 33:04.525
NOISY KIM MISSED CALL

713
33:10.280 --> 33:11.198
[door closes]

714
33:23.377 --> 33:24.420
[sighs softly]

715
33:35.597 --> 33:39.351
If I'm making you uncomfortable, I'll wait outside for a bit.

716
33:52.322 --> 33:54.992
The fact that you're with Mr. Yoon at this hour…

717
33:55.075 --> 33:56.326
shows how much he trusts you.

718
33:56.410 --> 33:59.329
[low tense music playing]

719
34:04.001 --> 34:06.920
Unfortunately, I don't trust you that much yet, Ms. Lee.

720
34:08.255 --> 34:10.299
You maintaining your low profile…

721
34:11.175 --> 34:13.802
is purely conjecture on Mr. Kim's part, after all.

722
34:13.886 --> 34:15.429
The feeling's mutual, sir.

723
34:16.680 --> 34:18.640
You should be very grateful that…

724
34:19.433 --> 34:20.684
Mr. Kim is your friend.

725
34:35.032 --> 34:36.366
It has a built-in voice recorder.

726
34:38.994 --> 34:42.206
When Ms. Han started working here, I gifted it to her.

727
34:44.666 --> 34:46.960
A secretary has to perfectly put every single word

728
34:47.044 --> 34:48.754
from their boss into action, after all.

729
34:49.505 --> 34:53.425
And you, Mr. Yoon, were infamous for being a difficult boss in that regard.

730
34:54.092 --> 34:55.636
I guess because of that,

731
34:56.470 --> 34:58.096
Ms. Han always kept this on her.

732
34:59.556 --> 35:01.767
If it was a gift, why do you have it?

733
35:03.519 --> 35:05.062
Do you think I went through her desk

734
35:05.145 --> 35:06.939
because I didn't have anything better to do?

735
35:07.022 --> 35:09.483
-So you weren't looking for her phone? -[sighs]

736
35:10.067 --> 35:11.235
I didn't know about that.

737
35:12.778 --> 35:15.489
I thought she was worried and called from a new number.

738
35:17.324 --> 35:18.158
That phone…

739
35:19.284 --> 35:20.786
do you know where it was found?

740
35:24.665 --> 35:25.666
So then…

741
35:26.416 --> 35:29.503
this contains information that will make me trust you, Ms. Lee?

742
35:34.800 --> 35:35.759
There's a condition.

743
35:39.429 --> 35:42.099
The preparations that you, Mr. Kim, and Mr. Park Min-hwan

744
35:42.182 --> 35:44.518
from Accounting Team Three have been working on,

745
35:44.601 --> 35:46.061
I want you to share them with me.

746
35:46.144 --> 35:48.730
That's out of the question. It's too dangerous.

747
35:49.314 --> 35:51.066
As I'm sure you all know,

748
35:51.149 --> 35:53.485
people talk a lot inside the chairman's office.

749
35:54.611 --> 35:57.364
I'm willing to share some of those conversations,

750
35:57.447 --> 35:58.907
provided I'm not compromised.

751
36:00.659 --> 36:01.869
You'll want to brace yourself.

752
36:02.578 --> 36:04.329
Things could get really dangerous.

753
36:04.997 --> 36:07.583
And if you were put in harm's way, this guy right here…

754
36:10.627 --> 36:12.713
Well, he won't just sit by and watch.

755
36:12.796 --> 36:15.257
I'm afraid I've got too much on my plate right now…

756
36:16.258 --> 36:17.759
to avoid any danger.

757
36:30.731 --> 36:33.025
Sorry… are you being threatened?

758
36:33.442 --> 36:34.443
Someone stalking you?

759
36:39.156 --> 36:40.908
They always wear the same shoes

760
36:42.075 --> 36:43.660
and stand in front of my apartment.

761
36:43.744 --> 36:45.954
[tense music playing]

762
36:47.915 --> 36:50.667
They seem to be keeping an eye on me to see what I know.

763
36:52.002 --> 36:54.087
[upbeat suspenseful music playing]

764
36:54.171 --> 36:55.631
[phone buzzes]

765
36:55.714 --> 36:57.883
TAKE CARE OF LEE HYE-JUNG FIRST

766
36:57.966 --> 37:00.093
[beeping]

767
37:01.762 --> 37:04.389
[footsteps thudding in distance]

768
37:04.473 --> 37:06.016
[Hye-jung] It also seemed like a threat,

769
37:06.099 --> 37:08.518
saying I would end up like Ms. Han if I were to talk.

770
37:09.186 --> 37:11.563
If the police hadn't found me on that phone,

771
37:11.980 --> 37:13.815
I'm sure that threat would still stand.

772
37:16.151 --> 37:18.737
I'll check to see if it's the same prick that's going after Park Min-hwan.

773
37:18.820 --> 37:20.489
The prick after Park Min-hwan…

774
37:20.989 --> 37:22.449
Han Eun-young's killer…

775
37:23.992 --> 37:25.202
The prick wearing the same shoes…

776
37:27.245 --> 37:28.622
They could all be one guy.

777
37:28.705 --> 37:30.123
[Wan-gu] What'll we do about Ms. Lee?

778
37:30.207 --> 37:32.960
Shouldn't we stop questioning her and put her under protection instead?

779
37:37.756 --> 37:40.050
KIM SI-HYUN

780
37:40.133 --> 37:41.343
LEE HYE-JUNG

781
37:48.392 --> 37:49.476
YOON NA-JUNG

782
37:50.811 --> 37:54.064
Detective Kim, let's stay on Ms. Lee till we question her again.

783
37:54.147 --> 37:55.107
Yes, sir.

784
37:55.857 --> 37:58.860
Man, Kang really came through for us, huh?

785
37:59.444 --> 38:01.238
[Wan-gu] I'll bet Yoon Yi-jun's totally clueless

786
38:01.321 --> 38:03.490
as to what kind of person she really is.

787
38:03.573 --> 38:04.491
[scoffs]

788
38:05.492 --> 38:08.829
Detective Kang, on the other hand, knows what Yoon Yi-jun's like.

789
38:12.290 --> 38:15.127
[Seok-jin] The more that she knows, the more she'll be biased.

790
38:18.547 --> 38:19.673
One way or another.

791
38:25.804 --> 38:28.932
I go for a run now and then when I have a lot on my mind.

792
38:29.850 --> 38:31.810
Would you like to go for a run with me?

793
38:31.893 --> 38:32.894
No. [sighs]

794
38:36.231 --> 38:38.567
Please don't worry about Ms. Lee too much, sir.

795
38:40.235 --> 38:42.154
You've assigned a security detail to her.

796
38:42.237 --> 38:45.407
Mr. Kim will look after her, and the police…

797
38:47.075 --> 38:48.952
will also keep an eye on her for now.

798
38:54.124 --> 38:55.125
Do you regret it?

799
38:57.335 --> 38:58.378
Sometimes.

800
38:59.629 --> 39:00.756
You can bet

801
39:00.839 --> 39:03.508
that that money won't be used for anything good.

802
39:04.009 --> 39:06.178
-That's the kind of place Taekang is. -[somber pensive music playing]

803
39:06.261 --> 39:07.846
It's where bad motives…

804
39:09.389 --> 39:10.724
pass as justification.

805
39:12.267 --> 39:14.227
I was worried that those motives

806
39:14.978 --> 39:16.855
might hurt people unrelated to them.

807
39:20.484 --> 39:22.110
That's why I started looking for it.

808
39:25.322 --> 39:26.490
But I was careless…

809
39:30.202 --> 39:31.411
and acted rashly.

810
39:37.959 --> 39:39.628
If I had just covered it up

811
39:41.838 --> 39:43.465
when I first found out about it,

812
39:45.175 --> 39:47.511
I wonder if things wouldn't have gotten so bad.

813
39:58.230 --> 39:59.272
[sighs]

814
40:00.357 --> 40:02.859
Do you wanna know why I left the army when I did?

815
40:09.449 --> 40:11.118
[soldier 1] No footprints under the ridge.

816
40:11.576 --> 40:13.078
[soldier 2] Copy that. Advancing.

817
40:14.204 --> 40:15.872
[Jae-hee] I was taught that life was a journey

818
40:15.956 --> 40:17.874
one takes with a trustworthy friend.

819
40:20.335 --> 40:23.547
And Sergeant Go was both a brother-in-arms and my superior.

820
40:24.381 --> 40:26.550
When Jin-hyung was just over three months old,

821
40:26.883 --> 40:29.052
we were deployed on a hostage rescue mission.

822
40:30.303 --> 40:31.596
-[explosion] -[soldiers gasp]

823
40:32.389 --> 40:33.723
[soldiers groan]

824
40:38.395 --> 40:39.479
[gunfire]

825
40:39.563 --> 40:41.481
[tense music playing]

826
40:43.775 --> 40:45.193
[gunfire]

827
40:52.701 --> 40:53.618
[rustles]

828
40:54.202 --> 40:55.036
[nervous gasp]

829
40:57.038 --> 40:58.290
Please let me live.

830
40:59.708 --> 41:00.834
[Sergeant Go] Kang Jae-hee!

831
41:07.424 --> 41:10.051
-[squelches] -[Jae-hee gasps]

832
41:10.927 --> 41:12.596
[soldier 1] Shots fired. Check it out.

833
41:12.679 --> 41:14.472
-[Sergeant Go groaning] -[breathing heavily]

834
41:15.098 --> 41:16.016
Sergeant Go!

835
41:16.099 --> 41:17.642
[groans, breathing heavily]

836
41:18.185 --> 41:19.936
Staff Sergeant. [grunts]

837
41:20.020 --> 41:22.105
I'm so glad… you're okay.

838
41:22.189 --> 41:24.024
[gasping]

839
41:24.858 --> 41:25.692
[gasps]

840
41:27.485 --> 41:29.070
No, no, don't!

841
41:29.154 --> 41:30.363
Sergeant Go!

842
41:30.780 --> 41:32.240
[screams] No!

843
41:32.741 --> 41:34.242
Sergeant Go!

844
41:34.618 --> 41:37.829
Sergeant Go! Sergeant Go! [crying]

845
41:37.913 --> 41:39.247
Sergeant Go…

846
41:40.457 --> 41:41.875
[screams] No!

847
41:41.958 --> 41:42.792
ARMY GO JAE-DEOK

848
41:42.876 --> 41:44.085
[Jae-hee] Just because…

849
41:44.753 --> 41:46.004
I hesitated for a second,

850
41:46.087 --> 41:47.505
Sergeant Go ended up…

851
41:48.340 --> 41:49.257
dead.

852
41:50.300 --> 41:52.219
And there was nothing I could do about it.

853
41:52.302 --> 41:54.554
[somber music playing]

854
41:54.638 --> 41:56.806
I dreamed of that moment a thousand times.

855
41:58.099 --> 41:59.309
ROK ARMY SPECIAL WARFARE COMMAND 7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

856
41:59.392 --> 42:01.228
But not even in my dreams…

857
42:02.687 --> 42:04.439
could I save Sergeant Go.

858
42:10.654 --> 42:11.821
That's why I ran away.

859
42:16.326 --> 42:17.911
But I regret it a little bit.

860
42:20.872 --> 42:23.458
At the least, I shouldn't have run away from it like that.

861
42:26.169 --> 42:27.170
[inhales]

862
42:29.589 --> 42:31.841
Took me a while to find my way again.

863
42:32.342 --> 42:34.219
I swore to the sergeant that…

864
42:34.302 --> 42:36.429
I would work hard to make the world a better place

865
42:36.513 --> 42:38.014
for Jin-hyung to grow up in.

866
42:44.938 --> 42:46.690
Don't be like me and run away from it, sir.

867
42:47.857 --> 42:49.442
You know what you need to do.

868
42:50.318 --> 42:53.238
And knowing what you need to do is proof, in and of itself,

869
42:53.738 --> 42:55.573
that you're actually on the right path.

870
43:03.873 --> 43:05.375
[inhales deeply]

871
43:05.458 --> 43:06.793
Special Forces…

872
43:08.295 --> 43:09.796
you trying to make me feel better?

873
43:13.216 --> 43:15.468
I felt like I might not get a chance to later.

874
43:16.845 --> 43:18.513
We don't know what life will bring us.

875
43:19.306 --> 43:20.307
Well…

876
43:22.350 --> 43:23.935
that actually does help a lot.

877
43:26.354 --> 43:27.856
We might become enemies…

878
43:29.566 --> 43:31.735
and you might actually come to hate me, sir.

879
43:41.369 --> 43:42.454
[sighs softly]

880
43:44.956 --> 43:46.333
[inhales deeply]

881
43:46.708 --> 43:48.043
There's no way.

882
43:49.336 --> 43:51.338
[gentle music playing]

883
43:55.133 --> 43:56.217
[Yi-jun sighs]

884
44:03.224 --> 44:04.184
Remember…

885
44:07.395 --> 44:08.480
when we met…

886
44:09.689 --> 44:11.316
and I said that I would have fallen for you

887
44:11.399 --> 44:12.400
if you were a woman?

888
44:13.818 --> 44:14.778
[inhales]

889
44:15.820 --> 44:18.156
So, would you really have fallen for me…

890
44:19.949 --> 44:21.242
if that was the truth?

891
44:23.411 --> 44:24.245
No way.

892
44:29.250 --> 44:30.085
[inhales]

893
44:31.836 --> 44:33.505
It's pointless to assume things.

894
44:34.672 --> 44:36.925
Like if you're a woman or if you're a man…

895
44:39.344 --> 44:40.428
when you're just…

896
44:42.222 --> 44:43.431
just you.

897
44:46.434 --> 44:47.519
That's true.

898
44:49.521 --> 44:52.607
It is pointless to make assumptions.

899
45:16.423 --> 45:17.257
[Na-jung scoffs]

900
45:18.216 --> 45:20.301
What kind of situation is this?

901
45:24.264 --> 45:26.391
[laughing]

902
45:33.314 --> 45:35.316
[Yi-jun] Isn't it obvious?

903
45:37.026 --> 45:39.279
I just want to buy a suit for my personal secretary.

904
45:39.362 --> 45:40.905
Why do I need your permission?

905
45:40.989 --> 45:42.740
'Cause I'm the one you're buying it for.

906
45:43.199 --> 45:45.660
I promise I'll dress accordingly for the banquet, sir.

907
45:45.743 --> 45:46.995
That's why you're getting a suit.

908
45:47.078 --> 45:50.290
-[sighs] -This event is extremely important.

909
45:50.373 --> 45:52.959
I have the opening speech, I'm getting an award.

910
45:53.376 --> 45:55.378
And there will be a lot of photos taken.

911
45:55.462 --> 45:58.590
So… if my personal secretary were an ugly individual,

912
45:58.673 --> 46:00.508
my image would also take a hit, wouldn't it?

913
46:04.179 --> 46:07.932
[Jae-hee sighs] If they take my measurements, I'm gonna get caught.

914
46:08.391 --> 46:09.642
[Yi-jun] It's part of your job.

915
46:09.726 --> 46:11.853
Take your measurements… now!

916
46:11.936 --> 46:13.021
Yeah. It's just…

917
46:13.688 --> 46:15.315
I find it a little overwhelming, sir.

918
46:15.732 --> 46:17.108
[Si-a] Gorgeous.

919
46:20.445 --> 46:21.529
What do you mean?

920
46:22.822 --> 46:23.865
This suit.

921
46:23.948 --> 46:25.825
Some folks would kill to wear one of these.

922
46:28.369 --> 46:29.454
"Overwhelmed"?

923
46:30.079 --> 46:31.706
[scoffing chuckle]

924
46:31.789 --> 46:32.957
That's not…

925
46:33.708 --> 46:35.960
a reasonable excuse when you're dealing with a chaebol.

926
46:38.421 --> 46:39.631
Or…

927
46:43.134 --> 46:45.345
[whispers] …is there a reason you don't want your measurements taken?

928
46:45.428 --> 46:47.680
[tense music playing]

929
46:57.357 --> 46:59.400
Measure me. It's fine.

930
47:02.111 --> 47:03.196
Please turn around.

931
47:07.700 --> 47:08.701
[tailor coughs]

932
47:10.119 --> 47:12.121
Ms. Lee, are you gonna keep standing there?

933
47:12.580 --> 47:13.414
Mm-hmm.

934
47:14.123 --> 47:15.542
That's uncomfortable.

935
47:15.625 --> 47:16.543
Oh, no, I'll be okay.

936
47:16.626 --> 47:18.127
You're making me uncomfortable.

937
47:18.211 --> 47:20.004
What, with that moral code of yours?

938
47:20.755 --> 47:23.925
You must be the only person who asks his boss to step outside

939
47:24.509 --> 47:26.094
'cause they make you uncomfortable.

940
47:26.719 --> 47:27.554
[sighs]

941
47:29.681 --> 47:32.684
All right, fine. Let's step outside.

942
47:36.187 --> 47:37.021
[Si-a] Mm.

943
47:41.776 --> 47:42.777
[door opens]

944
47:44.487 --> 47:45.572
[door closes]

945
47:47.365 --> 47:48.575
It is what you think it is.

946
47:48.658 --> 47:51.077
-[tense music playing] -Let Mr. Yoon know if you must.

947
47:51.160 --> 47:52.328
Although…

948
47:52.412 --> 47:54.914
if something were to happen to him 'cause you ratted me out,

949
47:54.998 --> 47:56.666
you'll bear full responsibility.

950
47:57.166 --> 47:58.835
Hmm. Are you threatening me?

951
47:59.669 --> 48:00.920
I'm asking for your help.

952
48:01.462 --> 48:03.798
For now, due to my professional obligations,

953
48:03.881 --> 48:06.301
I have to keep this secret, but once the dust settles,

954
48:06.884 --> 48:08.886
I'll come clean and tell him myself.

955
48:16.269 --> 48:17.353
[keyboard key clicks]

956
48:34.162 --> 48:37.165
I don't think I can make this work before the shareholder meeting.

957
48:38.207 --> 48:40.460
Can we… postpone the wedding?

958
48:41.294 --> 48:42.712
Aren't you forgetting something?

959
48:43.504 --> 48:46.007
Like the five Ws and one H, or cause and effect?

960
48:46.090 --> 48:48.384
I didn't think you'd be interested in my situation.

961
48:48.468 --> 48:49.969
Mm-hmm. I'm not.

962
48:51.804 --> 48:54.432
[chuckles softly] Spare me the details then.

963
48:54.515 --> 48:56.643
I'm sorry, but I won't delay the wedding.

964
48:58.227 --> 49:00.980
Well, if you can't delay it, let's move it forward.

965
49:01.773 --> 49:02.649
Let's do it now.

966
49:02.732 --> 49:04.359
[soft scoff] I don't know.

967
49:04.901 --> 49:07.070
I'm a little too interested in your love affair

968
49:07.153 --> 49:08.655
to do anything right now.

969
49:09.947 --> 49:11.908
-[elevator dings] -[elevator doors open]

970
49:15.828 --> 49:18.081
[footsteps approaching]

971
49:19.374 --> 49:23.169
So then, let's hold our wedding in the season that suits me the best.

972
49:26.130 --> 49:27.298
I love you too.

973
49:27.382 --> 49:29.759
[tense pensive music playing]

974
49:34.055 --> 49:35.473
What do you think you're doing?

975
49:35.556 --> 49:36.974
Oh, are you all set?

976
49:56.202 --> 49:58.871
-[Yi-jun sighs] -I'll be going home, sir.

977
49:58.955 --> 49:59.872
Uh…

978
50:00.957 --> 50:02.875
Okay, I have something I need to say.

979
50:03.710 --> 50:06.504
You know how I don't accept a single misunderstanding, right?

980
50:06.587 --> 50:07.588
You see,

981
50:08.256 --> 50:11.300
the adverb "too" in the phrase "I love you too" implies

982
50:11.384 --> 50:13.553
a shared sentiment with something said in the preceding statement.

983
50:13.636 --> 50:14.929
-But I know-- -[Jae-hee] I get it.

984
50:15.012 --> 50:16.556
I interrupted a private moment.

985
50:17.890 --> 50:18.891
I'm sorry, sir.

986
50:21.644 --> 50:23.855
No, that's not what I'm trying to say at all.

987
50:26.274 --> 50:27.358
[sighs]

988
50:37.410 --> 50:38.703
[reporters clamoring]

989
50:38.786 --> 50:41.205
-[reporter 1] You're looking wonderful! -[camera shutters clicking]

990
50:41.998 --> 50:43.124
[reporter 2] Please look this way.

991
50:43.750 --> 50:44.709
Hi.

992
50:44.792 --> 50:45.668
[reporter 3] Over here!

993
50:47.754 --> 50:48.880
Hi.

994
50:48.963 --> 50:51.257
-[reporters clamoring] -[camera shutters clicking]

995
50:55.219 --> 50:57.722
Mr. Yoon. He's the best-looking one out there.

996
51:02.393 --> 51:04.312
[Da-woon] You don't look too bad today yourself.

997
51:04.395 --> 51:06.355
Why is it that he bought you that suit when I did all the work?

998
51:09.734 --> 51:12.487
[light orchestral music playing]

999
51:14.280 --> 51:16.866
[indistinct chatter]

1000
51:19.619 --> 51:20.495
[reporter] Oh, he's here.

1001
51:20.578 --> 51:24.290
[camera shutters clicking]

1002
51:26.292 --> 51:29.587
Oppa, if you cheat on your wife, you'll go to hell.

1003
51:31.339 --> 51:32.173
Smile.

1004
51:36.719 --> 51:39.680
If that's all it takes, then I guess I'll see you down there.

1005
51:39.806 --> 51:41.015
[chuckles softly]

1006
51:41.390 --> 51:43.392
Why are you so cranky?

1007
51:44.143 --> 51:46.646
Mr. Kang giving you a hard time?

1008
51:58.366 --> 52:01.536
[phone buzzing]

1009
52:02.578 --> 52:03.788
SEOK-JIN

1010
52:07.375 --> 52:09.544
[automated voice's indistinct chatter]

1011
52:10.878 --> 52:12.380
[line ringing]

1012
52:13.548 --> 52:16.300
I could give you a raise and a better performance bonus,

1013
52:17.009 --> 52:18.761
but you'd rather stay with Yi-jun?

1014
52:19.262 --> 52:20.596
[sighs] Yeah.

1015
52:20.680 --> 52:22.598
Hmm, I guess he treats you better than I do.

1016
52:22.682 --> 52:24.100
I'm so jealous.

1017
52:25.268 --> 52:27.436
Why are you doing this to me, Ms. Lee?

1018
52:28.855 --> 52:30.481
Just tell me what you want and be done with it.

1019
52:30.565 --> 52:32.942
Oh, didn't I tell you right from the start?

1020
52:33.025 --> 52:34.360
I thought I made it clear.

1021
52:35.278 --> 52:36.320
[Si-a] We should be friends.

1022
52:36.404 --> 52:39.824
And I made it clear from the start that I don't want that. I really don't.

1023
52:39.907 --> 52:42.243
You know, I don't often make male friends.

1024
52:43.953 --> 52:45.621
A female friend is different, though.

1025
52:49.876 --> 52:52.461
-[uneasy music playing] -I'll head up first, ma'am.

1026
52:52.545 --> 52:54.755
Mm, you don't have to be so cold.

1027
52:55.840 --> 52:58.759
-[sighs] -Come on, let's be friends.

1028
53:01.554 --> 53:02.513
I'd rather not.

1029
53:02.597 --> 53:04.181
I'll let him know your secret.

1030
53:06.183 --> 53:07.393
That you're actually a woman.

1031
53:07.476 --> 53:08.978
[dramatic music sting]

1032
53:10.062 --> 53:11.731
Good luck fooling everyone else.

1033
53:13.566 --> 53:14.984
[Na-jung] Who's fooling who?

1034
53:18.863 --> 53:19.822
Curious, are we?

1035
53:20.281 --> 53:22.283
[tense music playing]

1036
53:22.909 --> 53:24.035
Right, so Mr. Kang--

1037
53:24.118 --> 53:25.036
Let's do it.

1038
53:26.037 --> 53:26.871
Friends.

1039
53:29.790 --> 53:30.708
Okay.

1040
53:30.791 --> 53:32.627
So, who was fooling who?

1041
53:33.753 --> 53:36.672
Hmm… Well, Mr. Kang…

1042
53:40.301 --> 53:42.345
[chuckles softly] He's just so cute.

1043
53:43.346 --> 53:47.183
[sighs dreamily] Too bad I was going to cheat on Yi-jun…

1044
53:47.725 --> 53:48.976
except I got caught red-handed.

1045
53:49.060 --> 53:50.436
[breathes nervously]

1046
53:50.519 --> 53:53.731
Well, at least you're straightforward, dear sister-in-law.

1047
53:54.857 --> 53:57.360
There's no point in lying to you with your network.

1048
53:58.319 --> 53:59.320
He is cute, isn't he?

1049
54:03.699 --> 54:04.700
Well, he's not ugly.

1050
54:06.285 --> 54:08.955
If you're going to fool around with him, do it properly…

1051
54:10.581 --> 54:12.166
and I'll keep it out of the news.

1052
54:12.583 --> 54:16.837
[scoffing chuckle] I'd be grateful, but what do you get out of that?

1053
54:17.672 --> 54:19.632
Would screwing poor Yi-jun make you feel good?

1054
54:21.717 --> 54:22.927
Oh, no, you two.

1055
54:23.552 --> 54:25.304
Looks like you got caught cheating.

1056
54:25.972 --> 54:26.889
Too bad.

1057
54:27.431 --> 54:28.766
[chuckles]

1058
54:32.228 --> 54:34.230
[low tense music playing]

1059
54:37.108 --> 54:40.027
Brother dear, how could you…

1060
54:40.111 --> 54:43.781
hire such a bottom-rung degenerate to be your secretary?

1061
54:44.782 --> 54:45.825
Be careful.

1062
54:45.908 --> 54:48.703
Nothing's more humiliating than your fiancée

1063
54:48.786 --> 54:50.329
getting caught fooling around.

1064
54:52.331 --> 54:54.959
They introduced a sudden tax hike policy.

1065
54:55.418 --> 54:58.754
I hope… you didn't mess with the hotel shares, did you?

1066
54:59.880 --> 55:00.798
It's my hotel.

1067
55:00.881 --> 55:03.050
Why don't you try saying that to Father's face?

1068
55:06.679 --> 55:07.513
Coming?

1069
55:14.562 --> 55:16.564
It's almost Mom's death anniversary.

1070
55:16.647 --> 55:18.899
[Na-jung] Try acting like that in front of Father then.

1071
55:18.983 --> 55:19.984
[Si-a sighs]

1072
55:20.484 --> 55:23.237
Things were about to get interesting. How disappointing.

1073
55:23.696 --> 55:24.530
Just wait.

1074
55:26.282 --> 55:28.159
'Cause the main event…

1075
55:29.702 --> 55:31.579
hasn't even started.

1076
55:36.751 --> 55:39.170
[suspenseful music playing]

1077
55:50.973 --> 55:52.558
[Hye-jung] That police car I saw yesterday,

1078
55:52.641 --> 55:53.601
I saw it again today.

1079
55:55.227 --> 55:57.897
And this morning's security guards? I saw them later.

1080
55:58.939 --> 56:01.776
So, why do I have to report every little detail

1081
56:01.859 --> 56:02.943
to you like this, Mr. Kim?

1082
56:03.027 --> 56:03.944
Firstly,

1083
56:04.445 --> 56:06.906
you didn't mention that you were being tailed, client of mine.

1084
56:06.989 --> 56:08.115
[Si-hyun] And second,

1085
56:08.199 --> 56:10.785
you turned down my offer to take you home tonight.

1086
56:10.868 --> 56:14.163
Thirdly, your lawyer's five minutes away from arrival.

1087
56:15.581 --> 56:16.415
Arrival where?

1088
56:16.874 --> 56:19.251
[inhales] I think you already know.

1089
56:23.130 --> 56:24.965
I'm heading over with some dinner,

1090
56:25.049 --> 56:27.384
so maybe you should take the time to hide the body.

1091
56:28.594 --> 56:30.679
[both chuckle softly]

1092
56:32.848 --> 56:33.682
[phone beeps]

1093
56:33.766 --> 56:36.185
-[ominous music playing] -[keypad beeping]

1094
56:39.605 --> 56:41.440
[breathing heavily]

1095
56:49.573 --> 56:51.909
I refuse to let those two screw with my head.

1096
56:51.992 --> 56:53.410
So just tell it to me straight.

1097
56:55.913 --> 56:58.207
Ms. Lee approached me first, and then…

1098
56:58.290 --> 56:59.250
Ms. Yoon Na-jung showed--

1099
56:59.333 --> 57:00.543
I don't care about that!

1100
57:00.626 --> 57:02.086
I don't need you to give me a report.

1101
57:02.878 --> 57:04.964
Just tell me about you. What's going on in your head?

1102
57:05.047 --> 57:06.298
Why aren't you interested?

1103
57:07.675 --> 57:08.926
She's your fiancée…

1104
57:09.426 --> 57:10.427
so you should be interested.

1105
57:10.511 --> 57:12.972
You're marrying her. She should be your priority.

1106
57:14.014 --> 57:14.849
That way…

1107
57:15.933 --> 57:17.560
I would not get the wrong idea.

1108
57:18.978 --> 57:19.812
What?

1109
57:26.360 --> 57:27.403
[knocking on door]

1110
57:32.324 --> 57:33.200
[exhales shakily]

1111
57:38.330 --> 57:41.333
[low tense music playing]

1112
57:45.379 --> 57:46.380
[door closes]

1113
57:50.634 --> 57:51.635
[soft gasp]

1114
57:57.766 --> 57:58.684
What is that?

1115
57:59.393 --> 58:00.477
It's nothing, sir.

1116
58:02.062 --> 58:03.063
Let it go.

1117
58:07.151 --> 58:08.944
[dramatic music sting]

1118
58:09.028 --> 58:11.322
-[tense unsettling music playing] -[gasps]

1119
58:11.405 --> 58:12.615
[dramatic music sting]

1120
58:14.617 --> 58:16.035
[breathes shakily]

1121
58:16.493 --> 58:17.703
[Da-woon] The event is starting soon, sir.

1122
58:17.786 --> 58:18.621
You should…

1123
58:19.288 --> 58:20.122
What's going on?

1124
58:20.206 --> 58:21.540
Nothing's going on.

1125
58:21.624 --> 58:23.792
You go on without me. I'll take care of things here.

1126
58:25.336 --> 58:28.505
[breathing heavily]

1127
58:32.468 --> 58:33.844
She's late today.

1128
58:34.720 --> 58:36.222
[Captain Park] Why isn't the light coming on?

1129
58:37.097 --> 58:38.557
What do you think, Mr. Profiler?

1130
58:38.641 --> 58:40.809
There can be two causes of routine delays.

1131
58:40.893 --> 58:43.020
External intervention, or…

1132
58:43.103 --> 58:44.313
[inhales]

1133
58:44.396 --> 58:46.649
-…an internal threat. -[tense music sting]

1134
58:47.775 --> 58:48.776
Run.

1135
58:49.735 --> 58:52.154
-[suspenseful music playing] -[choking]

1136
59:11.966 --> 59:13.968
[panting]

1137
59:15.135 --> 59:16.220
[young Yi-jun] Mom!

1138
59:16.887 --> 59:18.389
Mom, wake up!

1139
59:18.472 --> 59:19.723
[breathing heavily]

1140
59:19.807 --> 59:22.476
[host] We'll be kicking off the 2026 Korea Leadership

1141
59:22.559 --> 59:24.103
and Management Awards ceremony

1142
59:24.186 --> 59:27.898
with an opening speech from Taekang Group's Mr. Yoon Yi-jun.

1143
59:28.857 --> 59:29.900
[exhales]

1144
59:31.402 --> 59:34.738
[phone buzzing]

1145
59:37.950 --> 59:38.867
Yeah.

1146
59:40.494 --> 59:41.620
Wait, Ms. Lee…

1147
59:42.955 --> 59:43.872
She what?

1148
59:43.956 --> 59:45.791
[Si-hyun] Is everything all right over there?

1149
59:45.874 --> 59:49.962
Nothing's going on. You go on without me. I'll take care of things here.

1150
59:51.213 --> 59:52.298
[breathes shakily]

1151
59:52.381 --> 59:54.049
[Da-woon] Sir, you have to go on now.

1152
59:56.593 --> 59:59.346
[engine revving]

1153
01:00:00.180 --> 01:00:02.016
-[suspenseful music continues] -[panting]

1154
01:00:06.770 --> 01:00:09.106
-[engine revving] -[gasps]

1155
01:00:13.319 --> 01:00:15.738
[music intensifies]

1156
01:00:20.826 --> 01:00:22.703
[music fades]

1157
01:00:24.913 --> 01:00:27.750
We have to catch him! [panting]

1158
01:00:30.127 --> 01:00:31.378
[Yi-jun panting]

1159
01:00:36.425 --> 01:00:38.844
[soft bright music playing]

1160
01:00:46.393 --> 01:00:47.561
What are you doing?

1161
01:00:51.732 --> 01:00:53.400
Everything went pitch-black…

1162
01:00:56.528 --> 01:00:58.364
and all I could think about was you.

1163
01:01:00.657 --> 01:01:01.742
Could we just…

1164
01:01:03.994 --> 01:01:05.496
stay like this for a while?

1165
01:01:07.247 --> 01:01:09.917
[mellow music playing]

1166
01:01:24.681 --> 01:01:26.767
[Jae-hee] I took advantage of your desire

1167
01:01:27.393 --> 01:01:29.019
to have me around…

1168
01:01:31.063 --> 01:01:32.564
and I'll keep doing it,

1169
01:01:33.190 --> 01:01:34.274
so please don't…

1170
01:01:38.570 --> 01:01:39.988
come any closer.

1171
01:01:51.375 --> 01:01:54.294
[closing theme music playing]

1172
01:02:10.269 --> 01:02:12.312
SPECIAL THANKS TO CHOI HEE-JIN, JUNG YOO-MIN FOR THEIR SPECIAL APPEARANCE

1173
01:02:12.396 --> 01:02:14.398
[handcuffs rattling, click]

1174
01:02:16.400 --> 01:02:19.027
Please wake up! Lee Hye-jung! Are you people insane?

1175
01:02:19.111 --> 01:02:20.404
[Seok-jin] Detective Kang's theory holds water.

1176
01:02:20.487 --> 01:02:22.990
[Na-jung] Did you come onto him first? I really had no idea.

1177
01:02:23.073 --> 01:02:24.491
-[Da-woon] How about a blind date? -[Jae-hee] Is she pretty?

1178
01:02:24.575 --> 01:02:25.409
Is she pretty?

1179
01:02:25.492 --> 01:02:27.035
-Is she pretty? -[Yi-jun] "Is she pretty?"

1180
01:02:27.119 --> 01:02:27.953
[scoffs]

1181
01:02:28.036 --> 01:02:30.080
[Si-hyun] The heir to Taekang and his same-sex secretary.

1182
01:02:30.164 --> 01:02:32.583
Yoon Yi-jun's fallen for you, right? That's not gonna work out.

1183
01:02:32.666 --> 01:02:36.128
[Jae-hee] This situation's dangerous. You need to start facing reality.

1184
01:02:36.211 --> 01:02:37.254
[Si-hyun] You should have been prepared for this.

1185
01:02:37.337 --> 01:02:40.382
[Yi-jun] If I were to break off the wedding, would you start to like me?

1186
01:02:40.466 --> 01:02:41.800
[Jae-hee] That won't ever happen.

1187
01:02:41.884 --> 01:02:43.051
-[Yi-jun] I… -Careful, sir!

1188
01:02:43.135 --> 01:02:44.636
[Yi-jun] I like you, Kang Jae-hee.
